id: pm-chahyq
title: "Improvement ledger: measured properties of pm carry a recorded time series, because a ceiling proves a number did not grow and can never prove a change made it smaller"
description: ""
type: Feature
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[3]: measurement,ratchet,self-improvement
created_at: "2026-08-05T18:09:39.606Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-06T21:01:21.544Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-06T21:01:20.864Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-06T21:01:20.864Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 480
acceptance_criteria: "Every declared measurement retains an append-only series of observations with the commit and the timestamp that produced each, not just the current ceiling and a measured_on date; A read surface answers 'how has this population moved since it was filed' without replaying git history by hand; The series is derived from recorded observations, never hand-edited, and survives compaction; The existing ratchet keeps failing on growth; the ledger adds the falling half of the signal"
parent: pm-o0sqz5
risk: low
confidence: high
resolution: completed
expected_result: "Audited improvement observations retain append-only revision/time provenance and expose bounded trends through SDK, CLI, and MCP without weakening ratchets."
actual_result: "Implemented an audited improvement ledger with immutable metric contracts, finite numeric validation, storage-boundary provenance validation, lock-scoped concurrent-safe mutation, retry idempotency, content identities, bounded trends, typed SDK/MCP integration, token-bounded CLI recovery, and reusable workspace mutation primitives."
