comments[7]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-06T17:01:56.721Z","harness:codex","Implementation start 2026-08-06: all-status duplicate search for improvement ledger, measurement series, observations, and ratchets found pm-chahyq as the canonical feature. Active scope is a reusable SDK/CLI measurement primitive with append-only observations, bounded deterministic reads, commit/timestamp provenance, and tracker-backed acceptance. The blocked candidate-synthesis and cycle-contract children remain open and unclaimed."
  "2026-08-06T17:22:59.898Z","harness:codex","Implementation evidence: added an audited workspace improvement ledger with content identities, retry idempotency, immutable metric contracts, Git/caller/unversioned revision provenance, bounded reads, and direction-aware trends; exposed it through SDK, CLI stats, MCP, contracts, completions, and documentation."
  "2026-08-06T19:59:37.662Z","harness:codex","Quality correction: the release token-surface gate rejected 15 new flat stats flags (3355 bytes versus 1437). Replaced them with one strictly validated --analytics JSON adapter while retaining all typed SDK/MCP fields; the 91-surface agent token gate now passes without raising budgets or adding completeness waivers."
  "2026-08-06T20:12:14.557Z","harness:codex","Final verification: exact coverage passed across 441 files and 6,902 tests at 100% statements (49461/49461), branches (35933/35933), functions (10115/10115), and lines (47921/47921). TypeScript, ESLint, duplicate detection, 100% docstrings, contracts, SDK surface, package boundaries, SDK parity, token/context/tracker gates, zero-vulnerability audits, and temporary packed npx/direct-SDK/bunx acceptance passed. Timing budgets passed in a clean isolated sample; later host-load samples were invalidated by unrelated system contention without changing budgets."
  "2026-08-06T20:35:36.186Z","harness:codex","Review round 1: CodeRabbit produced 11 actionable exact-head findings spanning concurrency-safe audited writes, storage validation, finite numeric contracts, bounded history efficiency, invalid timestamp handling, CLI/schema recovery text, public changelog content, PM changelog linkage, and portable tests. Reopened and claimed only these four canonical items while addressing their own PR feedback."
  "2026-08-06T20:58:30.703Z","harness:codex","Review remediation verified: added lock-scoped mutateWorkspaceJsonWithHistory so ledger read/validate/append/write/history execute under one workspace lock; concurrent alpha/beta append test retains both observations; all thresholds are finite; revision_source is storage-validated; CLI unknown-field recovery lists accepted keys; public API docstrings restored."
  "2026-08-06T20:58:34.669Z","harness:codex","Post-review exact verification: 441 files and 6,903 tests passed at 100% statements (49476/49476), branches (35951/35951), functions (10122/10122), and lines (47936/47936). TypeScript, ESLint, zero-clone JSCPD, 100% docstrings, package boundaries, SDK parity, contracts, token/context/tracker/gate registries, docs, secrets, and zero-vulnerability production audit pass. Import timing is separately limited by current host load and no budget was changed."
learnings[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-06T20:12:03.614Z","harness:codex","A broad typed analytics surface must not become a broad agent-facing help surface: the 91-surface token gate caught 15 flat flags, and one strictly validated JSON adapter preserved capability while restoring the command budget without waivers."
  "2026-08-06T20:58:31.338Z","harness:codex","Audited singleton writers need a lock-scoped transform API, not a locked final write: acquiring only after a read leaves an invisible lost-update race even when every individual write and history append is atomic."
